{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775245113-KTWtrBBTELMcccXHDNY0","role":"assistant","created":1775245127,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found the relevant 2-year Treasury note auction data for Q4 1987 (the year of Black Monday which was October 19, 1987). Let me extract the auction amount tenders accepted for each 2-year note auction in Q4 1987:\n\nFrom the 1988 March bulletin (covering Oct-Dec 1987):\n- October 21, 1987 auction: $9,255 million accepted\n- November 18, 1987 auction: $9,269 million accepted  \n- December 22, 1987 auction: $9,286 million accepted\n\nSo Q4 1987 average = (9,255 + 9,269 + 9,286) / 3 = 27,810 / 3 = $9,270 million\n\nNow I need to find the data for Q4 1988, Q4 1989, and Q4 1990. Let me check the other bulletins.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_64b8813631a86997","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -n -i \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1989_03.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
